Language English

Book PlaceDiningRoom Ordered No Keep Looped
	Triggered By @talkedToBen When @talkedToBenCount >= 2
	
	Page Locked
		Triggered By @ExploreHall1ViaDiningRoomLocked
		
		Text """
			The door is filthy. You check the knob, but it's locked:  you'll need a key to get in.
		"""
		
		Mark Unread
		Exit
	End Page Locked

	Page OpenDoor
		Triggered By @TalkToBackyardBen When @TalkToBenCount >= 2
		
		Add TileDiningRoom, TokenBackyardBenPassive, TokenDoorDiningRoom!
		Remove TokenExploreDiningRoomViaBackdoor, TokenBackyardBenBefore

		Text """
			<<Ah! Here's the key,>> Benjamin exclaims. He steps up to the door
			and unlocks it. A surprising amount of dirt falls as he pushes it
			open.

			The door creaks open and you see what looks like the servants'
			dining room. The room makes the yard look orderly. Heaps of rubbish
			and broken glassware are strewn about the room.

			Place the {c:TileDiningRoom} tile and door as indicated, then remove
			this Explore token.
		"""
		
		exploredDiningRoom = true
		
		// we want a clear event name for the name of the target investigator,
		// not some wacky constructed name
		// we raise an event to have EventChosenInvestigator assigned
		Trigger @ChooseInvestigator
	End Page OpenDoor
	
	Page Kitchen
		Add TokenExploreKitchenViaDiningRoom!
		
		Text """
			To the right, a doorway opens to the kitchen. Place an Explore token
			as indicated.
		"""
		
	End Page Kitchen

	Page OtherExplores
		Add TokenExploreBasementFirst!, TokenExploreHall1ViaDiningRoomLocked!

		Text """
			Two other doors lead farther into the house. Place Explore tokens
			as indicated.
		"""
	End Page OtherExplores
	
	Page FluxStabilizer
		Add TokenSearchDiningRoomFluxStabilizer

		Text """
			An odd-looking device sits on the table. Place a Search token as
			indicated.
		"""
	End Page FluxStabilizer
	
	Page Paper
		Add TokenSearchDiningRoomPaper!
		
		Text """
			There's a box in the corner that was packed carelessly. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		// we do this because if they haven't found the journal,
		// there will be another page after this one
		If foundJournal Then Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
	End Page Paper
	
	Page Journal
		Page Is Visible When Not foundJournal
		
		Text """
			As you walk into the house, you remember the book in the driveway. You glance back toward the gate as you step inside. Move 1 space into the {c:TileDiningRoom}.
		"""
	End Page Journal
End Book PlaceDiningRoom

Book SearchDiningRoom Ordered No Keep Looped

	Page StartFluxStabilizer
		Triggered By @SearchFluxStabilizer When Unread
		If testMode Then Trigger @AskAboutGate
	
		Prolog "A small device with gears, hoses, and lights sits on the table."
		Button "Search"
	
		Text """
			As you reach down to pick it up, the device sparks and booms,
			generating a pressure wave that pushes all
			investigators--including you--1 space away from the
			device.

			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} recovers first and stands back up. As
			they approach the device, nothing happens. Move
			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} into the device's space.

			The other investigators are wary of this device and will avoid it at
			all costs. When it is not held by {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, no
			other investigator can stay in its space. Fear makes them
			move away immediately.
		"""
		
		// wanderers are the cultists who seem to be coming from the secret
		// passageway off the study.
		wandererMax = #heros - exploredBackyardNicely
		If wandererMax < 1 Then wandererMax = 1
		
		wandererFrequency = 2
	End Page StartFluxStabilizer
	
	Page Finn
		Page Is Visible When #HeroFinnEdwards
		
		Text """
			Finn Edwards starts to come to, not sure at first where he is:  he
			is on the ground where he fell. As his vision clears, he feels
			different. He feels... off. Finn can no longer use his special
			ability.

			As he starts to push himself up, he puts his hand down in the wrong
			place. Hard. Pain. When he looks at what he hit, he gains the
			{c:QItemBrassKnuckles} Common Item. As he plays with them, they make
			him feel more confident. Improve Finn's {strength}.
		"""
	End Page Finn
	
	Page Kate
		Page Is Visible When #HeroKateWinthrop
		
		Text "Will Kate pick up the {c:QItemFluxStabilizer}?"
		
		Test "Yes" Or "No" Set katePicksUp
		If katePicksUp Then Goto KatePicksUp
		Goto KateDoesNotPickUp
	End Page Kate

	Page KatePicksUp
		Text """
			Kate is overjoyed that she will have a {c:QItemFluxStablizer} again,
			especially one this powerful.
			
			Looking at it, she calms down and loses her focusing anger. Kate no
			longer becomes Focused when she is attacked.
			
			Kate says to the others, <<This device can repel monsters. I don't
			expect I'll need it here, but mine broke this morning
			and I didn't know how I'd find another.>>
		"""
		
		Mark Paper Read
		kateHasFluxStabilizer = true
		Exit
	End Page KatePicksUp
	
	Page KateDoesNotPickUp
		Text """
			Kate quietly seethes to herself at the unfairness:  <i>That
			thing should be mine.</i>
			
			Kate becomes Focused.
		"""
	End Page KateDoesNotPickUp

	Page Paper
		Text """
			There is a piece of paper next to the device: instructions. It's
			called a <<{c:QItemFluxStabilizer},>> and it repels monsters.
			<<MOnSTERS!?>> you erupt loudly.

			Everyone turns to look at you.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page Paper

	Page Puzzle1
		Page Is Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchFluxStabilizer When Unread And StartFluxStabilizer Is Read

		Prolog """
			There seems to be a
			control panel. Maybe you can restart it? You reach down and begin
			to fiddle with the buttons and dials.

			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} may attempt the puzzle using {lore}.
		"""
		Button "Attempt puzzle"
		
		Puzzle PuzzleFluxStabilizer Set passFluxStabilizerPuzzle
		If passFluxStabilizerPuzzle Then Goto GetFluxStabilizer
		Goto DontGetFluxStabilizer
	End Page Puzzle1

	Page Puzzle2
		Triggered By @SearchFluxStabilizer When Puzzle1 Is Read
		
		Prolog """
			Maybe if you randomly flipped a few more buttons or turned a few
			more dials, it will do something.
			
			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} can attempt it again using {lore}.
		"""
		
		Puzzle PuzzleFluxStabilizer Set passFluxStabilizerPuzzle
		If passFluxStabilizerPuzzle Then Goto GetFluxStabilizer

		Mark Unread
		Goto DontGetFluxStabilizer
	End Page Puzzle2

	Page DontGetFluxStabilizer
		Text """
			It still just sits there. Doing nothing. The hoses aren't moving,
			the lights are off, and 
		"""
		Exit
	End Page DontGetFluxStabilizer

	Page GetFluxStabilizer
		Text """
			The device begins humming quietly.

			Discard this search token, then place the {c:QItemFluxStabilizer}
			common item in its place.

			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} can drop or pick up this item, but
			cannot trade it to another investigator. When the
			{c:QItemFluxStabilizer} is on the floor, any investigator who moves
			or is moved into its space immediately moves 1 space away from the
			device. Move toward the {c:TileDiningRoom} if possible; you do not
			need to evade monsters when moving this way.
			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} is immune to this effect.

			When {c:EventChosenInvestigator} holds this item, add 1 additional
			movement to their move actions.

			This information can be reviewed in the app.
		"""

		Exit
	End Page GetFluxStabilizer

	Page GetFluxStabilizer2
		Add TokenBackyardBenAfter!
		Remove TokenBackyardBenPassive
	
		Text """
			Benjamin walks through the door into the {c:TileDiningRoom}. Move
			the purple man token as indicated.

			As he walks in he says, <<I heard a noise. This house
			can be dangerous with everything in disarray. Please be careful.>>

			He seems to be holding something in his hand.
		"""
		
		If Not exploredBackyardNicely Then Text """
			Benjamin walks briskly through the door snapping, <<What are you
			folks doing in here?!>> Move the purple man token as indicated.

			He seems to have something in his hand.
		"""
	End Page GetFluxStabilizer2

	Page PaperInBox
		Triggered By @SearchDiningRoomPaper
		
		Prolog "There's a yellowed scrap of paper in the box."
		Button "Search"
		
		Add QItemEvidenceDiningRoom
		Remove TokenSearchDiningRoomPaper

		Text """
			The paper is old, yellowed, and dry. When you pick it up, a corner
			breaks off. The writing is faded but you can make out a few phrases.

			<<... this Saturday, the children will...>>

			<<... everything is ready, but my daughter doesn't know...>>

			<<Blood will... chapel... altar>>

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceDiningRoom} Unique Item, gain 2 {clue}, and
			discard this Search token.
		"""
		
	End Page PaperInBox
End Book SearchDiningRoom


Book ExploreBackDoorLocked Ordered No Keep Looped

	Page TurnKnob
		Prolog "
			The door that closed behind you looks larger and more
			solid from inside.
		"	

		Button "Open door"

		Text "You reach for the knob. Test {strength} or {agility}."

		Test Quota 20 Set passWhoCares
	End Page TurnKnob

	Page ShakeDoor
		Prolog """
			No matter how hard you try, the knob just won>t turn.
			Looking closer, you see a light peeking between the door
			and its jam. <i>Maybe I can shake it open?<i> you think
			to yourself.
		"""
		Button "Shake door"
	
		Text """
			You grab the knob again and begin shaking it violently. Test
			{strength} or {will}.
		"""
	
		Test Quota 20 Set passWhoCares
	End Page ShakeDoor
	
	Page HitDoor
		Prolog "
			No matter how hard you shake it, the door doesn't budge.
			And you might have pulled something in your right arm.
			Maybe you can knock it down? You also begin to wonder
			if you should move on. Or knock it down.
		"
		Button "Break it down"

		Text "
			You muster up your strength and prepare to break the door down
			with your shoulder. Test {strength} or {lore}.
		"

		Test Quota 20 Set passWhoCares
	End Page HitDoor

	Page PickLock
		Prolog "
			The third or fourth time you hit door, something in your
			shoulder pops and it hurts. Bad. You feel the panic setting in.
			<i>Why won>t this door open?</i> you ask yourself.
			
			Take 1 facedown damage ({strength} negates).

			<<Hey, is this a hairpin?>> you ask out loud. One of the other
			investigators turns to look at you.
		"
		Button "Pick lock"

		Text """		
			As you work the hairpin into the lock, you wonder
			why it was in your pocket. Test {agility} or {influence}.
		"""

		Test Quota 20 Set passWhoCares
	End Page PickLock

	Page UnlockDoor
		Prolog """
			You can feel the tumblers, but nothing moves. Eventually, the
			hairpin bends too much to be of use. <i>Maybe this really is
			a waste of time,</i> you consider. <i>Wait, I have that key.</i>

			If you have the	{c:QItemBrassKey}, ...
		"""

		Text """
			You pull out the key and look at it for a moment before putting
			it into the lock...
			Test {strength} or {observation}.
		"""
	
		Button "Unlock door"

		Test Quota 20 Set passWhoCares
	End Page UnlockDoor

	Epilog 
        Remove TokenExploreBackDoorLocked

		Text """
			Well, you try to put the key into the lock but it doesn't fit,
			no matter how hard you try. You look at the key and try again.
			And again. And again. Dejected and out of ideas, you turn away
			from the door. <<I guess we'll have to find another way out,>>
			you say to no one in particular. Someone mutters, <<Yeah.>>
		
			Discard this explore token.
		"""
	End Epilog
End Book ExploreBackDoorLocked


Book ExploreKitchen Ordered No Keep Looped
	Page Start
		Prolog """
			The swinging door doesn't look like it will hold up to much use, so
			you'll need to be careful.
		"""
		Button "Push through door"

		Remove TokenExploreKitchenViaDiningRoom
		
		Text """
			Compared to the dining room, the kitchen looks clean. The
			cupboards are empty. A couple of barrels of wine and a
			half-packed box have been left behind. Maybe the rest of
			the house will be as easy to clean as this room.

			<i>Still, cleaning is in the details</i>, you think to
			yourself. <i>And there are lot of details here.</i>

			Remove this Explore token.
		"""
		
		exploredKitchen = true
		$MythosKitchen = true
	End Page Start
	
	Page Cutlery
		
		Add TokenSearchKitchenCutlery!

		Text """
			You notice a few pieces of cutlery have been left on the
			counter; place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page Cutlery
	
	Page Box
		Add TokenSearchKitchenRandom!

		Text """
			Next to you is a box that looks like it was filled in a
			hurry. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Trigger @moveAfterExplore
		Exit
	End Page Box
End Book ExploreKitchen

